cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Variant Calling Benchmarking Across Sequencing Depths
message: If you use this pipeline or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abdelmoghni
    given-names: Hossam Hatem
    affiliation: Nile University
abstract: >-
  A reproducible GATK Best Practices pipeline that quantifies how sequencing
  depth affects germline variant calling accuracy. The GIAB HG002 whole-exome
  library is downsampled to 2x, 10x, 40x and 60x on chromosome 22, called with
  HaplotypeCaller, and benchmarked against the GIAB v4.2.1 truth set with hap.py.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - variant-calling
  - benchmarking
  - GATK
  - hap.py
  - genome-in-a-bottle
  - next-generation-sequencing
license: MIT
date-released: 2025-12-01
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Best practices for benchmarking germline small-variant calls in human
      genomes
    authors:
      - family-names: Krusche
        given-names: Peter
    journal: Nature Biotechnology
    volume: 37
    start: 555
    end: 560
    year: 2019
    doi: 10.1038/s41587-019-0054-x
